        <div class=3D"section">
            <h2>Publications</h2>
           =20

            <div class=3D"publication">
                <a style=3D"display: contents" href=3D"https://sophie-kerga=
ssner.github.io/phase-aligned-metamers.html">
                    <img class=3D"publication-teaser" src=3D"https://sophie=
-kergassner.github.io/img/PhaseAlignedMetamers_Teaser.jpg">
                </a>

                <div class=3D"publication-description">
                    <h3 class=3D"publication-title">
                        <a href=3D"https://sophie-kergassner.github.io/phas=
e-aligned-metamers.html">
                            It=E2=80=99s Not Just a Phase: Creating Phase-A=
ligned Peripheral Metamers
                        </a>
                    </h3>

                    <p class=3D"publication-authors">
                        <span class=3D"author-highlight">Sophie Kerga=C3=9F=
ner</span>, Piotr Didyk
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-venue" style=3D"margin-top: 10p=
x;">
                        <em>ACM SIGGRAPH 2026</em>
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-summary">
                        We present a method for enhancing the perceived qua=
lity of foveated images by extrapolating local image statistics, such as in=
tensity, orientation and especially phase, from coarse to fine scales. In p=
articular, we demonstrate that correct phase alignment across space and sca=
les is crucial for achieving perceptually convincing image quality.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>




            <div class=3D"publication">
                <a style=3D"display: contents" href=3D"https://sophie-kerga=
ssner.github.io/depth-from-motion-and-disparity.html">
                    <img class=3D"publication-teaser" src=3D"https://sophie=
-kergassner.github.io/img/DepthFromMotionAndDisparity_Teaser.png">
                </a>

                <div class=3D"publication-description">
                    <h3 class=3D"publication-title">
                        <a href=3D"https://sophie-kergassner.github.io/dept=
h-from-motion-and-disparity.html">
                            The Impact of Blur on Motion Parallax and Binoc=
ular Disparity
                        </a>
                    </h3>

                    <p class=3D"publication-authors">
                        <span class=3D"author-highlight">Sophie Kerga=C3=9F=
ner</span>, Piotr Didyk
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-venue" style=3D"margin-top: 10p=
x;">
                        <em>IS&amp;T Electronic Imaging (Human Vision and E=
lectronic Imaging) 2026</em>
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-award">
                        =F0=9F=8F=85 Best Student Paper Award
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-summary">
                        We examine the impact of blur on the depth perceive=
d by motion parallax and evaluate the findings in comparison to our <a href=
=3D"https://sophie-kergassner.github.io/depth-in-periphery.html">previous f=
indings</a> on the impact of blur on stereoacuity.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>



            <div class=3D"publication">
                <a style=3D"display: contents" href=3D"https://sophie-kerga=
ssner.github.io/depth-in-periphery.html">
                    <img class=3D"publication-teaser" src=3D"https://sophie=
-kergassner.github.io/img/DisparityInPeriphery_Teaser.jpg">
                </a>

                <div class=3D"publication-description">
                    <h3 class=3D"publication-title">
                        <a href=3D"https://sophie-kergassner.github.io/dept=
h-in-periphery.html">
                            Towards Understanding Depth Perception in Fovea=
ted Rendering
                        </a>
                    </h3>

                    <p class=3D"publication-authors">
                        <span class=3D"author-highlight">Sophie Kerga=C3=9F=
ner</span>, Taimoor Tariq, Piotr Didyk
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-venue" style=3D"margin-top: 10p=
x;">
                        <em>ACM SIGGRAPH 2025</em>
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-summary">
                        We demonstrate that stereoacuity is remarkably resi=
lient to foveated rendering and remains unaffected with up to 2=C3=97 stron=
ger foveation than commonly used. To this end, we design a psychovisual exp=
eriment and derive a simple perceptual model that determines the amount of =
foveation that does not affect stereoacuity.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>



            <div class=3D"publication">
                <a style=3D"display: contents" href=3D"https://sophie-kerga=
ssner.github.io/hivefive360.html">
                    <img class=3D"publication-teaser" src=3D"https://sophie=
-kergassner.github.io/img/HiveFive360_Teaser.png">
                </a>

                <div class=3D"publication-description">
                    <h3 class=3D"publication-title">
                        <a href=3D"https://sophie-kergassner.github.io/hive=
five360.html">
                            HiveFive360: Extending the VR Gaze Guidance Tec=
hnique HiveFive to Highlight Out-Of-FOV Targets
                        </a>
                    </h3>

                    <p class=3D"publication-authors">
                        <span class=3D"author-highlight">Sophie Kerga=C3=9F=
ner</span>, Nina Doerr, Markus Wieland, Martin Fuchs, Michael Sedlmair
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-venue">
                        <em>ACM Mensch und Computer 2024</em>
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-award">
                        =F0=9F=8F=85 Best Paper Award (Honorable Mention)
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-summary">
                        We extend the gaze guidance technique <span style=
=3D"font-style: italic;">HiveFive</span> to guide users to out-of-FOV targe=
ts. Our technique is qualitatively and quantitatively evaluated in two user=
 studies. Our results show that HiveFive360 is effective in guiding users t=
o a target object, and diegetic, meaning that the scenic immersion of the s=
cene is preserved.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>


           =20
            <div class=3D"publication">
                <a style=3D"display: contents" href=3D"https://doi.org/10.2=
352/EI.2023.35.2.SDA-383">
                    <img class=3D"publication-teaser" src=3D"https://sophie=
-kergassner.github.io/img/SimulatedLightfield_Teaser.jpg">
                </a>

                <div class=3D"publication-description">
                    <h3 class=3D"publication-title">
                        <a href=3D"https://doi.org/10.2352/EI.2023.35.2.SDA=
-383">
                            Evaluating the Angular Resolution of a Simulate=
d Light Field Display in Regards to Three-Dimensionality, Motion Parallax a=
nd Viewing Experience
                        </a>
                    </h3>

                    <p class=3D"publication-authors">
                        <span class=3D"author-highlight">Sophie Kerga=C3=9F=
ner</span>, Jan Fr=C3=B6hlich
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-venue">
                        <em>IS&amp;T Electronic Imaging (Stereoscopic Displ=
ays &amp; Applications) 2023</em>
                    </p>

                    <p class=3D"publication-summary">
                        We show that the viewing experience of a multiview =
screen increases logarithmically with the presented number of views.
                        This rise stagnates at around 0.25=C2=B0 per view. =
Below 0.5=C2=B0 per view, participants prefer a common 2D display.
                    </p>

                    <!-- <a class=3D"publication-link" href=3D"https://doi.=
org/10.2352/EI.2023.35.2.SDA-383">Paper</a> -->
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>



